---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';

const TRAILHEAD_EMAIL = 'trailhead@theforestnetwork.earth';
---

<SiteLayout title="About">
  <article class="site-panel prose">
    <h1>About The Forest Network</h1>
    <p>
      The Earth has been calling her human children to remember how to be in relation to all
      things; to be in deep relation to ourselves, other human beings, and the more-than-human
      beings we share this corner of the galaxy with.
    </p>
    <p>
      The idea for The Forest Network came through the Muse as part of a soul revelation: two throbbing, fiery galaxies across
      the tapestry of space and myself between them and all the stars. Tapping into that primal energy, 
      being part of it. Arms outstretched wide and it all flowing into and through me. In connecting it 
      all I am connecting myself to <i>all of it</i>.
    </p>

    <h2>The Village</h2>
    <p>
      The Village is a private, invite-only messaging community for beings involved in nature & soul work, 
      and it is the first incarnation (of possibly many) of The Forest Network. It is non-commercial, non-monetised, and free. 
      It is based in Naarm, Australia, on the traditional lands of the Wurundjeri people, and is tended by 
      Evan Roth, Daniel McLean, and others. The Village is designed not to be a replacement for in-person connection, 
      but rather as a way to facilitate <i>more of it</i>.
    </p>

    <h2>Built to be private</h2>
    <p>
      The Village runs on the <a href="https://matrix.org/">Matrix protocol</a> on our own server in Australia, 
      and with federation turned off so your data is not shared with any other server. Direct messages and private
      channels are end-to-end encrypted. You access the Village through the Forest Network app,
      available for iOS and Android, or the Element X web client. Although the apps are available on the Apple and
      (soon) Google Play stores, you must first be invited to join the Village. This is to preserve the safety, focus, 
      and vitality of the Village.
    </p>

    <h2>Values</h2>
    <p>
      We are not affiliated with any one organisation but are connected to many. We are passionate about open source 
      software and believe in the fundamental right of users not to be manipulated and exploited by Big Tech. We 
      believe we are being called to dream the dream of the entire earth alongside all beings on it. We believe there 
      is a collective need for The Forest Network and for collective healing. 
    </p>

    <h2>Invitations</h2>
    <p>
      We are looking for people who are passionate about what The Forest Network is (and what it could be) to help us grow it. 
      There is space on our Council for people who feel called to that, and we are also looking for people to test beta releases 
      of the apps for iOS and Android. Is there some other way you feel called to help? Let us know!
    </p>

    <h2>Join us</h2>
    <p>
      If this calls to your heart, <a href="/village/join">find the trailhead</a> and tell us a
      little about yourself. Questions are always welcome: write to{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${TRAILHEAD_EMAIL}`}>{TRAILHEAD_EMAIL}</a>, or visit{' '}
      <a href="/village/support">Support</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .prose h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .prose p {
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
